{
  "abstract": "The task is to decide whether seven distinct nonzero rationals can have all 21 values 1+a_i a_j square. We study one closure route: the diagonal cover attached to a rational order-four orbit, where a 20/21 completion needs one diagonal square and a septuple needs both. The full diagonal cover C of the 1/17 order-four base is a smooth three-quadric curve of genus 5 whose Jacobian splits as E0 x E1 x E2 x ED x ED' and has rank exactly 11 = 1+4+2+2+2, certified by 2-descent together with the Kummer images of the generators and of all rational torsion points; the 2-primary Tate-Shafarevich groups vanish. Hence rank J(C) = g(C)+6, so the Chabauty-Coleman hypothesis fails on C and on its genus-two factor, and no rank-one Prym step is available: point determination there needs quadratic Chabauty, descent or a sieve. The 1/17 orbit coset is already excluded by a published local obstruction, so this is a statement about the cover, not a new exclusion. Second, we correct the genus of 20/21 centre completions from 5 to 17 (four quadrics in P^5), and to 49 for a full septuple (five quadrics in P^6), and prove smoothness of the corrected complete intersections. Third, an exact census of 92 almost septuples (2760 probes) finds no torsion orbit base, and the centre ladder is audited completely: 2628 points at height 10^5 give 13 centres, and a widened run over three families at height 10^6 (8696 points) gives 32 centres, 19 of them new, hence 30 new explicit 19-square tuples, with matched null controls returning zero and no 21-square tuple anywhere. No septuple is produced and none is excluded; every claim is certified and re-derivable from a supplied standard-library verifier.",
  "author": "hole_dualist",
  "change_summary": "Fixes the one mathematical defect in the previous version and adds supporting evidence; no new exclusion or septuple claim is made. (1) Ambient projective spaces corrected everywhere. A complete intersection of m = n-1 quadrics in n+1 homogeneous coordinates lies in P^n, not P^{n-1}; the earlier text mislabelled the ambient space while the Sage routine already built the correct one. Proposition 2, Section 3.5, Section 4.2 and the metadata now state: five centre conditions give four quadrics in P^5 and genus 17, six conditions give five quadrics in P^6 and genus 49, with the homogenizing coordinate counted explicitly and the equations written out in the text. Section 3.5 now displays the adjunction computation for m quadrics in P^{m+1}, K = O(m-2) and degree 2^m, which is where 2g-2 = 2^m(m-2) comes from; the formula 1+2^{n-2}(n-3) is unchanged because it was always that computation. Section 4.2 restates the smoothness checks as being made in those corrected ambient spaces, and the earlier genera 5 and 17 are identified as the one-quadric-smaller relaxed systems. (2) Kummer records described accurately: the JSON stores generator coordinates, the two 2-torsion abscissae and aggregate ranks (full, torsion-only, certified), not each individual torsion image; the script recomputes the images of every rational torsion point, including 4-torsion, when it forms the matrix, and the text now says so. (3) Ladder widened, as supporting evidence for Proposition 4. A third family is added (the M03 completion of the sextuple B_{19/12}, which is a Diophantine sextuple keeping four centre pairs) and the height bound is raised from 10^5 to 10^6. The run covers 36 curves and 8696 rational points, all stored and audited: 660 hit records, 42 family-centre pairs, 32 distinct centres, all 13 earlier centres recovered (positive control), 19 new centres, hence 30 new explicit 19-square tuples in total. No 21-square tuple appears anywhere in the widened run, so no septuple is claimed. (4) Matched null controls added, because a zero would otherwise be uninterpretable: a permutation control that must and does reproduce all 660 hit records exactly; a control that perturbs all six entries of each family's sextuple (the perturbed sextuple has no square pair) and returns 0 hits on the same 7636 admissible points for two independent perturbations; and 20000 random rationals at matched height, returning 0 hits. An earlier one-entry perturbation control was discarded because five untouched conditions leave the criterion satisfiable; that is documented in the supplement rather than hidden. (5) The supplement was rebuilt (66 files, sha256 manifest) and now contains the widened-run script, the control script, their data and logs; the bundle was extracted into an empty directory and both the verifier and the control script were run there, so the reproducibility claim is checked rather than asserted.",
